## Outer divisor, at BlockBound.sum_pairWeight_le
Source blobs BlockBound 6c68e80e3b1ea2b7983696716305493a37f2b1fd
(lines 221--249), BoxPartition 53f11966247a892d94cf688e8b366e887a92f641
(lines 332--389), LinkPairing a802533ca5a385d6f44c3254f1a4d600b28fc416
(one_le_xRowsIndex_and_saturationIndex), VolumeKernel
fc115f79a99192fc8ea0e72c2caa0bf2546b5cf0.
Fix the SAME S,c,j,t,p=(c',gamma) and V in the outer labelled-term
sum. Write k0=termElem c p, R=Ohat, g=S.gIdele, r=card(IndexBelow j).
Let Q=colLattice(xRows(frameGram k0))^*, B the sublattice using
only the first r rows, and M the class-V frame image from frameValueIndex.
B <= Q and [Q:B] is a positive natural by the level and termsOver
guard. Integral g gives gQ<=Q and gB<=B.

If o=[M:M intersect Q] is infinite, native o=0 and the desired
divisibility into zero is automatic (the inverse-power term is zero).
Otherwise finite quotient injection and multiplicativity give
  [M:M intersect gQ] = o [M intersect Q:M intersect gQ],
  [M intersect Q:M intersect gQ] | [Q:gQ].
The latter is exactly the order of the image of M intersect Q in Q/gQ.
Now compare the two chains from gB to Q, using multiplication by
the idele as an isomorphism B<=Q onto gB<=gQ:
  [Q:B][B:gB] = [Q:gQ][gQ:gB] = [Q:gQ][Q:B].
All indices are finite: B is generated by r columns, so B/gB is a
quotient of R^r/gR^r; gB has finite index in Q by the first chain.
Cancel [Q:B]>0 BEFORE estimating. Hence [Q:gQ]=[B:gB]
divides [R^r:gR^r]. This proves the exact required divisor
  frameValueIndex(c,k0,g,V) | [R^r:gR^r] frameValueIndex(c,k0,1,V).
No freeness, primitive basis or independence of the r generators is
needed here. The saturation condition belongs to the OTHER (inner)
count, not this argument. The abstract outer proof needs only the
positive xRowsIndex, not IsNearRep or agreement. Native labelled terms
supply it via termsOver and HasLevel. The certificate below separates
these two steps and makes an actual weighted count call; it is adapted
from the original inline proof, not an invocation of sum_pairWeight_le.

